    "result_text": "The build is green. The full test suite (`AcceptanceTest` \u2014 the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper) passes: **2 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner registration dates that default to the server's current date when omitted and round-trip in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (POST input) and `OwnerDto` (GET output) both gain a `LocalDate registrationDate`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to `@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** (the OfficeFloor build step) \u2014 After MapStruct maps the request to the entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when null, preserving any supplied date.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so this column is required for persistence; I updated all four dialects for consistency.\n\nMapStruct maps `registrationDate` by name automatically in both directions, so no mapper changes were needed. Jackson serializes `LocalDate` to ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, satisfying the response format requirement.\n\nBoth spec behaviors are verified by the tests: `coreDefaultsToToday` (omitted \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (supplied `2020-06-15` preserved).",
